            "created_at": "2025-09-18T22:45:41.713725+00:00",
            "notes": "In the final round, we\u2019re just fine-tuning a setup that has likely already delivered great results.\n\nIf in round 5 you chose [First Responder](item_30a5c70f-e0b5-489a-96ae-900f34c3823d) because your teammates didn\u2019t really need healing \u2014 and the situation hasn\u2019t changed \u2014 you can go for [Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1), which will give you better survivability.\nThat never hurts, especially in the final round, because (and I\u2019ll never get tired of saying this) your enemies are now potentially lethal.\nIf you\u2019re struggling to stay alive, this pick will definitely help.\n\nOn the other hand, if you went for [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4), then by this point, getting overhealth for yourself and for the teammate you res could very well change the outcome of the round.\n[Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1) is still a valid option \u2014 and so is [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4), of course \u2014 but it\u2019s up to you to evaluate and balance your choices based on the current situation.\n\nAt this stage, these three core powers are all useful \u2014 they\u2019re just useful in different ways.\n\nAs for abilities, the cherry on top is definitely [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b), In addition to the healing boost, it\u2019ll also come in handy when you spot enemies low on health.\n\n*Remember: as Mercy, pulling out the blaster is completely normal \u2014 but it\u2019s situational.\nA support-focused build is also meant to secure kills when the opportunity is right.\nI\u2019m cautious when talking about this, because I often see Mercys dive into enemy teams blaster-first, forgetting that, as effective as it can be, it\u2019s not meant for every situation.\nIf you\u2019re up against an experienced team, diving in like a missile looking for kills will cost you \u2014 big time.*\n\nNeedless to say, that\u2019s not the only possible option \u2014 the power system is designed to give you flexibility, so if you feel like something\u2019s missing, feel free to fill that last slot with whatever you need most.",
